NPC: drayman
LOCATION: lower
SCHEDULE: morning=lower_dray, midday=lower_dray, evening=lower_house_1, night=closed

TOPIC: default
  GATE: NOT topic_done(drayman, default) AND coat = plain
  TAG: drayman_plain
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  THE DRAYMAN: "Mind the traces, mister. The gelding bites when the salt air gets into his teeth."
  [He unhooks an oily trace-chain and drops it into the wagon bed with a heavy iron clatter.]
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v2
  THE DRAYMAN: "If you're looking for cart hire, I don't haul after four. Road's too slick along the mud flats."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: NOT topic_done(drayman, default)
  TAG: drayman_badge
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_medium_v1
  THE DRAYMAN: "Officer Corwin. If this is about axle grease on the turnpike, take it to the selectmen."
  WALTER CORWIN: "I'm asking about heavy wagon traffic, Giles."
  VOICE: trombone_cautious_medium_v2
  THE DRAYMAN: "Everything heavy in this town moves on my axles, Walter. And none of it breaks the peace."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: visit_count(drayman) >= 2 AND coat = plain
  TAG: drayman_repeat_plain_harness
  WEIGHT: 3
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_short_v1
  THE DRAYMAN: "Stand clear of the wheel hub, Walter. Axle grease doesn't wash out of plain wool."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: visit_count(drayman) >= 2 AND coat = plain
  TAG: drayman_repeat_plain_coal
  WEIGHT: 2
  [He heaves a split sack of anthracite onto the tailgate, wiping coal dust from his forehead.]
  VOICE: trombone_weary_medium_v1
  THE DRAYMAN: "Tide's coming up the ditch. Don't linger in the cartway if you don't have business."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: visit_count(drayman) >= 2 AND coat != plain
  TAG: drayman_repeat_badge_wagon
  WEIGHT: 3
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_short_v2
  THE DRAYMAN: "A police coat in the dray-yard makes the team nervous, Officer. Step outside the shafts."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: visit_count(drayman) >= 2 AND coat != plain
  TAG: drayman_repeat_badge_patrol
  WEIGHT: 2
  VOICE: trombone_dismissive_short_v2
  THE DRAYMAN: "I pay my wheel tax quarterly at the hall, Corwin. Odell knows where to find my books."

TOPIC: night_freight
  GATE: always
  TAG: drayman_freight
  LABEL: "Ask about heavy carts moving after midnight"
  TIME: 5
  WALTER CORWIN: "Someone hauled heavy cargo toward the Ophion ridge three nights ago. Well past midnight."
  [The drayman pauses with a leather trace in his fist, his jaw tightening.]
  VOICE: trombone_cautious_long_v1
  THE DRAYMAN: "Wasn't my team. My horses stay bedded down when the church bells hit eleven."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Did you hear them pass?"
  VOICE: trombone_haunting_medium_v1
  THE DRAYMAN: "Heard the iron rims on the frost gravel. Iron tires, heavy load, two-horse team.\n\nMoving fast, too. No lantern hanging from the axle.\nA man who hauls without a lantern on a turnpike isn't delivering flour."
  NOTEBOOK: drayman_night_wagon | "Giles the Drayman heard an unlit two-horse cart with iron tires racing toward the estate ridge past midnight three nights ago."
  EVIDENCE: unlit_night_cart

# Redundant-carrier backup: if mr_vale is missed, this supplies the same
# EVIDENCE the estate's freight discrepancy relies on downstream.
TOPIC: the_kitchen_stone
  GATE: evidence(service_work) AND NOT evidence(estate_freight)
  TAG: drayman_kitchen_stone
  LABEL: "Ask if he hauled stone to the estate kitchen wing"
  TIME: 5
  WALTER CORWIN: "Someone billed two carts of kitchen stone to the estate. Was that your team?"
  VOICE: trombone_cautious_medium_v1
  THE DRAYMAN: "Wasn't my axles, Walter, and that's the part that sticks with me."
  [He sets down a trace-chain, frowning at the memory.]
  VOICE: trombone_haunting_medium_v1
  THE DRAYMAN: "Everything heavy in this town moves through me or through Vale's manifests. That job did neither.\nThree carts went up that ridge road one morning and not one of them was mine or hired through the yard. Private drivers, private horses. I asked around after. Nobody local hauled it."
  NOTEBOOK: drayman_kitchen_stone_1 | "Giles the drayman confirms the estate's stone deliveries bypassed both his own team and the regular hire yard entirely — three carts, none locally hauled."
  EVIDENCE: estate_freight
